# Latin is the canonical form and is served bare, so /sr-lat is the same page twice. It
# was prerendered only so that typing the explicit prefix did not 404; a rewrite answers
# that better, by landing on the canonical rather than on a copy of it.
#
# A splat matches the rest of the path and :splat puts it back. 301 is the default.
/sr-lat/* /:splat

# Street pages are not prerendered -- 58,947 streets across three locales would be a
# hundred and seventy thousand files for URLs nobody reaches from outside the site. The
# fallback boots the app and it routes itself, but GitLab serves an unknown path as 404,
# so the status has to be asserted here. A splat is greedy and spans slashes, which is
# what carries the locale prefix.
/*/ulica/* /404.html 200
